.TH "CSDLC-PROOF" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-proof \- execute and retain an issue\-bound proof manifest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc proof ISSUE
\&csdlc proof \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc proof \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The semantic issue intent form is the current operational interface. It resolves issue identity and routes effects through the native semantic transaction owner.
.PP
\&Execute the retained plan validators through the native proof owner. Require admitted Cargo test arguments, current candidate bytes, successful nonzero test counts and fresh issue/worktree identity; retain actual outcomes in .csdlc/evidence/ISSUE/intent\-proof.json. This form rejects preview/execute overrides.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity and mutation guards.
.PP
\&Validators admit optional timeout_seconds from 1 through 300, default 300. The Unix owner creates an owned process group, captures stdout/stderr without blocking reader threads and bounds timeout/cancellation reap/drain to two additional seconds. Scoped serialized SIGINT/SIGTERM handling is restored after execution; receipts distinguish timed_out, cancelled and cleanup_complete and include actual elapsed time. Non\-Unix execution is explicitly unsupported. Proof refuses ignored untracked source/configuration outside native .csdlc artifacts and explicit disposable Rust cache roots. Those exemptions do not admit executable inputs: manifests, target sources and repository path dependencies must be tracked, and compiler dependency records reject excluded repository module/include inputs. Unsupported generated repository source is refused. Exact captured\-stream digests and bounded non\-lossless diagnostic excerpts are retained; sensitive\-key lines are omitted and repository/HOME paths replaced. Input drift or persistence refusal retains failed execution output without bypassing native evidence guards. The digest binds repository tracked bytes and declared validators; ambient HOME Cargo configuration, external toolchains and cached dependencies are not fully fingerprinted, so this is not hermetic build evidence.
.PP
\&Each validator receives a newly created private mode\-0700 temporary directory directly beneath its canonical bound worktree, named .csdlc\-validator\-tmp\-PID\-SEQUENCE. TMPDIR, TMP and TEMP all select that directory; parent temporary\-directory variables are ignored. The owner rejects noncanonical roots, roots owned by another OS user, group/world\-writable roots, and existing temporary paths (including symlinks). It never adopts an existing directory. Validators inherit only the explicitly reconstructed environment; this does not enable arbitrary environment passthrough.
.PP
\&The native Cargo target is WORKTREE/target/intent\-validation. Warm trusted same\-host dependency artifacts into that exact target before proof; do not change HOME or global Cargo configuration. Each validator outcome records temporary_root and cargo_target relative to its bound worktree. Temporary contents are removed after process cleanup, including failure and cancellation; cleanup_complete remains false if directory cleanup fails. Stream digests and proof outcomes remain durable. This controls standard temporary\-directory APIs, not arbitrary absolute paths written explicitly by validator code.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Runs the declared deterministic V3 command through bounded argv/request/evidence paths, normalizes its result and retains proof evidence. Requires authenticated invoking linked worktree ownership and exact generation/digest/head/common\-Git binding. Provider side effects, stale evidence and unsupported normalization fail closed. This is focused command proof, not broad semantic equivalence.
.SH OPTIONS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Execute an exact generated csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 request or its generated wrapper; stale snapshots fail closed.
.SH REQUEST
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&ProofRouteRequest and its typed binding/manifest/install fields are described in csdlc\-requests(1). Paths must stay within the authenticated bound issue evidence boundary; they are not arbitrary shell execution or filesystem destinations.
.SH EFFECTS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Executes declared subprocess and writes canonical proof artifacts on admitted execution; blocked proof is not successful validation.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.nf
\&csdlc proof 870
.fi
.PP
\&Fixture examples are parse\-checked; historical shadow/soak examples intentionally exercise their blocked behavior. Proof/install require actual current binding and valid referenced artifacts for success.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
\&Blocked reports use schema csdlc.v3.proof_route.v1 on stdout and a short stderr message with exit 2. Missing/stale binding, path escape, artifact digest mismatch and unauthorized execution remain blockers. Inspect status and findings before calling a proof complete.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
